comment_body:
This only clears `runningTask` when it still equals the originally submitted `task`, but `doRun` sets `runningTask` to the next queued merge before calling `next.run()`. If a shard callback throws on a later loop pass, `compareAndSet(task, null)` misses: that merge is never cancelled, its callback is lost, and `doClose` throws "partial reduce in-flight". The previous `runningTask.getAndSet(null)` handled this.

Repro: `batchedReduceSize=2`, 4 results, 3rd callback throws: 3 of 4 callbacks complete here, all 4 on `main`.

```java
@Override
public void onFailure(Exception exc) {
    synchronized (QueryPhaseResultConsumer.this) {
        onMergeFailure(exc);
        MergeTask current = runningTask.getAndSet(null);
        if (current != null) {
            releaseCurrentMergeResult();
            current.cancel();
        }
    }
}
